Split out of #175, which fixed the symptom (bin/karr and bin/karr-foundation stuck at 0.500 while lib/App/karr.pm went to 0.501) by hand. The cause is still open.

What is established:

- [@Author::GETTY] routes versioning through @Git::VersionManager, i.e. RewriteVersion::Transitional and BumpVersionAfterRelease::Transitional. dist.ini sets no `version_finder`, so plugin defaults apply.
- Those defaults are `[ :InstallModules, :ExecFiles ]` (RewriteVersion.pm:147, BumpVersionAfterRelease.pm:204), and @Basic -- which the bundle pulls in with only GatherDir/PruneCruft removed -- still provides ExecDir, so bin/ genuinely is in :ExecFiles.
- The Transitional subclass only wraps rewrite_version; it inherits the finder unchanged.
- assign_re / matching_re match a plain `our $VERSION = ${q(0.500)};` line, which is exactly what both scripts had.

By that reading the post-release bump should have rewritten bin/. It did not: 053b61e touched Changes and 54 files under lib/, nothing under bin/. Same for the release commit itself (56b48b8 left bin/ alone). The last time those two numbers changed was 2b29403, a hand edit by the maintainer.

So one of the established points above is wrong, and it is worth twenty minutes with `dzil dumpphases` / a debug-logged `dzil build` to find out which -- most likely candidates: :ExecFiles resolving empty at the time the bump plugin runs (plugin ordering: @Basic is added well before @Git::VersionManager), or munge_file bailing on those files for a reason its `log` line would name ("Skipping: ...").

Worth resolving because as it stands the bump is a manual step spread over three places, and the only thing that notices a miss is t/67-bin-version.t -- which did notice, but only after main had been red for a day. If the finder can be made to cover bin/, the class of bug disappears; if it cannot, the reason belongs in a comment next to those two lines so the next person does not re-derive it.

Explicitly NOT a request to change dist.ini blind: adding `version_finder = :ExecFiles` without knowing why the default failed would be cargo cult, and could narrow the finder and stop lib/ being bumped too.
