ROOT CAUSE FOUND. None of the three established premises is actually false -- the
finder genuinely works. The bug is one layer further down, in a mechanism the
ticket's investigation hadn't reached yet: the git-commit step that is supposed
to persist the bump is scoped by a second, independent, hardcoded allowlist
that @Git::VersionManager never wires to version_finder/:ExecFiles at all.

Evidence (installed modules on this machine, not docs):
- Dist::Zilla::Plugin::RewriteVersion 0.018, BumpVersionAfterRelease 0.018,
  Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::GETTY 0.318, Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Git::VersionManager 0.007.
- dist.ini sets no version_finder. Author::GETTY.pm:326-337: version_finder
  defaults to `[]` (no_cpan is false here), and GETTY.pm:653-656 only passes
  '*.finder' overrides into @Git::VersionManager's payload if @{version_finder}
  -- with it empty, NO finder override reaches RewriteVersion::Transitional or
  BumpVersionAfterRelease, so both fall back to their own class default
  [:InstallModules, :ExecFiles] (RewriteVersion.pm:147, BumpVersionAfterRelease.pm:204).
  ExecDir (from @Basic, untouched by GETTY's -remove list) does populate
  :ExecFiles from bin/.
- Verified live, not just read: dzil build -v in a throwaway clone shows
  RewriteVersion::Transitional actually processing bin/karr and
  bin/karr-foundation -- "updating $VERSION assignment in bin/karr" appears
  in the log, right alongside every lib/*.pm file. So :ExecFiles is NOT empty
  at runtime -- the "finder resolves empty" premise is ruled out.
- Ruled out the PkgVersion/package-statement insert-path premise too: both
  bin/karr and bin/karr-foundation already carry a literal
  our $VERSION = '0.500'; matching assign_re/matching_re exactly -- verified
  by running BumpVersionAfterRelease::_Util::matching_re("0.500") against the
  actual historical file content (git show 56b48b8:bin/karr): it matches. The
  insert/PkgVersion fallback (needs a package statement, per t/67's own
  comment) is irrelevant here since an existing assignment is found and
  rewritten, not inserted.

So BumpVersionAfterRelease would rewrite bin/karr and bin/karr-foundation on
disk during after_release, same as RewriteVersion does at build time. The
actual break is downstream, in @Git::VersionManager's hardcoded
"post-release commit" Git::Commit instance (VersionManager.pm ~140-149, POD
~276-282 -- the installed module's own documented default, not something
GETTY overrides):

    [Git::Commit / post-release commit]
    allow_dirty = Changes  (+ Makefile.PL/Build.PL if munged)
    allow_dirty_match = ^lib/.*\.pm$
    commit_msg = increment $VERSION after %v release
    (this message matches 053b61e exactly -- confirms that commit IS this
    plugin's output)

allow_dirty_match is a plain hardcoded string in configure(), never derived
from version_finder/BumpVersionAfterRelease.finder -- no code path extends it
to bin/. Not user-overridable through the GETTY bundle either: Git::Commit's
two instances ('release snapshot' and 'post-release commit') are added
directly, not through _payload_for(), and GETTY's plugin -remove matches by
class name only (Git::Commit), so removing it to reconfigure would kill both
commit steps, not just the wrong one.

Dist::Zilla::Role::Git::DirtyFiles::list_dirty_files($git, 1) (confirmed from
source) filters dirty files against that allowlist and silently drops
anything that doesn't match -- no warning, no fatal, it's just absent from
the list Git::Commit stages and commits. Mechanism: BumpVersionAfterRelease
bumps bin/karr's and bin/karr-foundation's $VERSION on disk correctly, but
the post-release commit step only ever stages lib/*.pm (+ Changes/
Makefile.PL/Build.PL) -- the bumped bin/ content is left as an uncommitted,
unstaged working-tree diff that dzil release finishes "successfully" without
ever surfacing. Whatever later touched that working copy (fresh clone, pull,
reset, or nobody noticing before the tree was reused) is why bin/ came back
showing 0.500 in every subsequent commit though nothing ever committed that
value on purpose.

NOT FIXED -- staying inside the audit boundary given for this task. Real
options for whoever picks this up next:
- Lowest risk: documented manual step -- after dzil release, before git push,
  check git status; if bin/karr / bin/karr-foundation show modified, fold
  into the release commit (git add + amend). Zero code risk, picks up what's
  already correct on disk. Just a habit, one step earlier than t/67 catching
  it after the fact.
- Real fix needs either patching upstream Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Git::VersionManager
  (not part of this repo) to extend allow_dirty_match by version_finder, or
  removing+reimplementing both Git::Commit steps by hand in dist.ini (GETTY's
